SIX NEW THINGS IN MADR TICKETS
What's new · November 17

Mark, here's what landed in the app today. It's all live now at madrtickets.com.


01 · PRICING
Know what every game is worth

Every upcoming game shows three things:
- Market: what buyers pay on Ticketmaster for seats near ours, all-in per ticket.
- List at: the price to enter when we list, with the strategy behind it.
- Vs the market: whether our price is too high, too low, about right, or not listed yet, plus how solid and fresh the data is.

It opens on games we still have seats for, and the filters narrow it to what needs action. It only advises: nothing here changes a Ticketmaster listing.

Prices update every Monday and Wednesday morning for now, from a read of Ticketmaster's listings in sections 101, 102 and 120.

Open Pricing: <%= pricing_url %>


02 · 3D SEAT MAP
See where every listing sits

A 3D model of sections 119, 120, 101 and 102, behind the Thunder bench basket, with every listing the research read for a game.
- Seats are colored by price, and ours (101, row DD, seats 1–3) glow orange.
- Tap a seat to see its listing, or tap a listing to light up its seats.
- Rows near ours show the exact seats; rows farther back light up as a whole.
- Drag to turn, pinch to zoom, and switch games from the menu.

Get there from the 3D button next to any game on Pricing.

Open the seat map: <%= seat_map_url %>


03 · MONEY
Payouts, squared away

The Money tab keeps track of who owes what, game by game. Right now we're all square.
- Every sale: what it sold for, my half of the payout, and what you've paid me.
- Venmo: your payments are pulled in from Venmo (read-only) and matched to the games they cover. Anything unclear waits for a quick review.
- Season tickets: my half of the season invoice, paid to you in installments, and what's left.

It's read-only: nothing on this page moves money.

Open Money: <%= money_url %>


04 · DASHBOARD
A home screen that leads with what matters

- Needs attention: anything to sell, deliver or confirm this week.
- Next unsold games & pricing: the next three games we have seats for, priced the same way as the Pricing page.
- Payouts: the balance and the three latest Venmo payments.

Open the dashboard: <%= root_url %>


05 · NEW LOOK
A new logo, and a sign-in page with some life

The new logo is a ticket with a basketball in the middle, in the app's own colors. On the sign-in page, the crowd does the wave around the arena, and our three seats glow orange in row DD.


06 · STAY SIGNED IN
Sign in once a year

Once you sign in on a device, the app remembers you for a year.

Put it on your iPhone's home screen: open madrtickets.com in Safari, tap Share, then Add to Home Screen. Already have it there? Delete it and add it again to get the new icon (you'll sign in once more).


